  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>PII confidentiality impact factors</h4><p>Assess each factor for the PII involved in this move, then decide the overall level. The factors are considered together: one may indicate low and another high, and the higher can override. Only the overall level is scored.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Overall level</th><th>Harm</th></tr><tr><td>Not applicable</td><td>PII the organization may release publicly</td></tr><tr><td>Low</td><td>would not cause harm greater than inconvenience, such as changing a telephone number</td></tr><tr><td>Moderate</td><td>financial loss due to identity theft or denial of benefits, public humiliation, discrimination, or potential for blackmail</td></tr><tr><td>High</td><td>serious physical, social, or financial harm, resulting in potential loss of life, loss of livelihood, or inappropriate physical detention</td></tr></table><p><i>Source: NIST SP 800-122 (2010), Sections 3.1 and 3.2. The factor scales are adapted from the guide's examples; the guide treats factor levels as illustrative and leaves the choice of factors to each organization.</i></p>",
  "RightSideEmbeddedUrl": "",
